/imud-*.tar.gz

# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/settings.json

# Local agent guidance (not shipped)
AGENTS.md
audit.md
continuespidrama.md
openfor1.9.0.md
issue23-coverage-plan.md

# notes/ is NOT a place to put things.  It held the engineering record until
# 2026-08-29, when it had reached 1.6 GB and 208 files and every live item in
# it turned out to be already visible in ROADMAP, an issue, or a commit
# message.  It was deleted, not migrated.
#
# The rule is now: open work is an issue, direction is docs/ROADMAP.md, and
# measurements and refuted theories go in the commit message they justify.
#
# The ignore stays as a guard: a scratch directory by that name will still
# never be committed, which is what makes re-creating one a private mistake
# rather than a public one.
notes/

# devbox/ is TRACKED — the Debian build/test container (devbox/README.md) is a
# contributor tool, not local tooling.  Nothing in the build, the packaging or
# CI refers to it and none of it ships in a .deb; it exists so that the suites
# and the .deb/systemd checks a non-Linux host cannot run have a home before a
# push.  Its build droppings land in ~/.cache/imud-devbox/, never in the repo.

# Cal file (machine-specific, not for version control)
cal.json

# libFuzzer reproducers, dropped in the CWD when a harness is run from the repo
# root.  They are findings, not test data: the ones worth keeping get committed
# under test/fuzz/corpus/<target>/ with a name that says what they reproduce
# (see cal_overflow_finite).  Left ungitignored they sit in `git status`
# forever and invite being staged by a wildcard.
crash-*
timeout-*
oom-*
leak-*

# macOS debug-symbol bundles from -g builds (never commit build artifacts)
*.dSYM/
*.imucap
# ...but fuzz corpus seeds are tracked test data, not build products
!test/fuzz/corpus/**/*.imucap

# Manufacturer datasheets are reference-only and never committed: they are
# copyrighted with no redistribution licence, and shipping them would make the
# source tarball non-DFSG-free.  See docs/datasheets.md — drivers cite a
# datasheet revision in their header comment instead.
#
# They live in docs/datasheet_pdf/, which the first rule ignores wholesale —
# extension and case stop mattering once the directory is the unit.
#
# The second rule stays as a backstop for a PDF dropped straight into docs/,
# and its extension is spelled case-insensitively on purpose: gitignore
# matching is case-SENSITIVE wherever core.ignorecase is false, which is every
# Linux checkout and this one, so a plain `docs/*.pdf` would miss the uppercase
# names some vendors ship (TDK's arrived as .PDF and showed up untracked).
# Given the 75 MB the repo once cost, this guard does not get to be fragile.
datasheet_pdf
docs/*.[pP][dD][fF]
# ...but docs/math.pdf is generated in-tree from docs/math.md and IS tracked.
!docs/math.pdf

# debian build artifacts (dpkg-buildpackage)
/debian/tmp/
/debian/.debhelper/
/debian/files
/debian/*.substvars
/debian/*.debhelper
# dh_installdeb writes <pkg>.debhelper.log, which /debian/*.debhelper does NOT
# match.  Only appears when the packages are built in-tree — CI builds them in
# a container, so nothing caught this until a local dpkg-buildpackage run.
/debian/*.debhelper.log
/debian/debhelper-build-stamp
/debian/imud/
/debian/imud-utils/
/debian/libimud0/
/debian/libimud-dev/
/debian/imud-signalk/
/debian/imud-mqtt/
/debian/imud-influxdb/
/debian/imud-mavlink/
/debian/imud-prometheus/
/debian/imud-wmm-data/

# Temporary per-unit calibration data captured during bench work (not source).
/temp-fit.json

# Built by `make imud.info` from the committed docs/imud.texi.  The .texi is
# tracked (make dist is `git archive HEAD`, so packagers must not need
# pandoc); the .info is a build product, and makeinfo IS a build dependency
# of the Debian package.
/imud.info

# apt-repo: the served site tree is generated by the workflow, never committed
/site/
# No .deb belongs on this branch at all — the apt pool lives on the orphan
# `apt-pool` branch (see apt/README.md).  Binaries committed here are
# permanent, which is what took the repo to 75 MB before 1.8.
/*.deb
